   328	## 7. Per-turn latency budget and measurement plan
   329	
   330	**Budget (design targets from F1, not measurements), reconciled [R4]:**
   331	
   332	- turn 0 (import, load, warm-up, first act) ≤ 20 s whole-call, so it draws
   333	  ≤ 19 s from the bank;
   334	- steady-state (turns 1–718) p99 ≤ 500 ms and max < 900 ms;
   335	- the steady-state excess over 1 s sums to ≤ 10 s over turns 1–718;
   336	- total bank draw per seat ≤ 29 s, leaving ≥ 31 s of the 60 s bank;
   337	- peak resident memory ≤ 6.5 GiB (§1), recorded.
   338	
   339	**Arithmetic estimate (unmeasured).**
   340	
   341	- The CPU path runs the padded trunk: 699 entity tokens + 2 player + 1 global +
   342	  4 scratch + 1 plan + 2 critic = **709 tokens**.
   343	- Linear FLOPs are about 2 × 4.22M trunk params × 709 ≈ 6.0 GFLOP.
   344	- Attention is about 8 layers × 4 × 709² × 256 ≈ 4.1 GFLOP.
   345	- That is ≈ 10 GFLOP per row. At an assumed 20–60 GFLOP/s single-thread fp32
   346	  it takes ≈ 170–500 ms.
   347	- The grammar heads run 7 unit slots batched over actors, then ≤ 10 market
   348	  positions: many small kernels whose cost is dispatch-bound, not
